      "title": "PaymentIQ launches Cashier Plus, giving payments teams no-code cashier layout control, persona previews and drop-off session replays",
      "text": "PaymentIQ launched Cashier Plus on 8 September, a three-part product built explicitly to remove engineering dependency from cashier changes. Builder configures amount-versus-bonus selection order, grid or list layouts, sliders or checkboxes, theming and branding. Preview simulates the player-side render against self-defined personas from VIPs to first-time depositors. Data surfaces drop-off points and provides anonymised session replays showing where and why a player abandoned checkout, then allows an experiment to be run and the winner promoted to production with 'no ticket, no release, no discussion'. The framing statistic is a cited case where 33,800 players opened the cashier but only 12,900 completed a deposit, leaving 20,900 unexplained. CEO Neil D'Souza said: 'By the time a player reaches the cashier, you've already won them. What happens next either keeps that win or throws it away.' Abner Fabbro of Rhino Entertainment Group cited linking payments to commercial incentives, such as bonuses on cheaper methods or conditional on three crypto deposits of EUR 50-plus in a week. Stake CFO Bo Li said self-serve testing across currencies and methods lowers cost per depositing player 'without buying a single additional click'. The lens point: cashier configurability is being repositioned from a platform feature to a commercial lever owned by payments teams, and the competitive benchmark is now no-code plus session-level evidence rather than a configurable template.",
