    "section": "North America",
    "title": "Fanatics Casino launches in Ontario as the province's 50th operator, with sportsbook and Alberta entry pushed to 2027",
    "meta": "Canadian Gaming Business | 1 Sep 2026",
    "summary": "Fanatics Casino launched in Ontario on 1 September, three weeks after Fanatics Betting & Gaming received its licences from the Alcohol and Gaming Commission of Ontario on 11 August. The casino soft-launched without fanfare as the province's 50th active operator. Ontario is FBG's first international market and first consumer-facing gambling operation outside the US. FBG President of Gaming Conor Grant told CGB that Fanatics Sportsbook will follow in Ontario in 2027 and that FBG will enter Alberta in 2027: 'Alberta is on the roadmap... It'll be 2027. We will land in Alberta.'",
    "why": "The sequencing decision is the useful part. A brand built on sports merchandise and a sportsbook-led US strategy chose to enter Ontario casino-first, because, as Grant put it, the market 'is predominantly casino' and casino could go live 'much quicker'. Nearly 90% of Ontario online handle and 80% of GGR comes from online casino, so the product order follows the market's actual revenue mix rather than the brand's natural strength. That is a localisation argument in its purest form and a direct rebuttal to lift-and-shift market entry. Grant's framing that Fanatics is 'treating it as an international market and not a 51st state' is the line worth repeating internally, since it implies separate content strategy, payments, bonusing and compliance rather than a configuration change. Entering as the 50th operator also says something about how crowded a mature regulated market becomes, and why differentiation has to come from product depth rather than brand alone.",
    "expanded": "On leading with casino, Grant said: 'We're two-and-a-half years into our journey in the US and we've been the fastest-growing there... This is our first foray into an international market.' A spokesperson said 'sports betting is not in our immediate plans and will come second'. FBG's casino operates in Michigan, New Jersey, Pennsylvania and West Virginia; Fanatics Sportsbook is live in 24 US jurisdictions and Fanatics Markets in 23 states. The Ontario portfolio spans hundreds of live dealer, slots and table games from Evolution, IGT and Playtech. Grant added: 'We don't come to play eighth or ninth in the market. We want to be a top operator.' Alberta's market opened on 13 July and FBG is not yet an AGLC registrant, so the 2027 timing implies a deliberate decision to prove the Ontario model before adding a second Canadian jurisdiction rather than racing to be early in a newly opened one. The count of 50 active operators includes all licensed commercial brands plus government-owned OLG, and Ontario's continued ability to attract entrants four years after opening remains the strongest available evidence for the competitive-market model over provincial monopoly.",
