    "meta": "GGRAsia | 9 Sep 2026",
    "summary": "UBS says Macau casino GGR averaged MOP 633m, about USD 78.34m, per day over 1-6 September, citing its own channel checks. The daily run-rate was up circa 4% year on year but down about 11.5% versus August's MOP 706m daily average, a steeper sequential fall than the roughly 5% average month-on-month seasonality decline seen between 2015 and 2019. UBS said mass daily revenue run-rate was down 10% to 12% month on month, while VIP volume run-rate was down 8% to 10%, at VIP hold of 3.0% to 3.3%. Consensus for full-September average daily GGR sits at MOP 650m to MOP 670m.",
    "why": "The sequential decline is running roughly twice the historic seasonal norm, and the mass segment is falling faster than VIP, which is the more concerning combination because mass is the volume base that underpins Macau's post-liberalisation model. The forward indicators are the part worth watching: of 31 hotels UBS tracks, five fewer are sold out year on year for October Golden Week, and average comparable hotel prices are down 22% year on year. Room rate softness of that magnitude ahead of the single most important demand week is a genuine leading signal rather than noise, and it follows a third consecutive month of annual GGR decline after 16 months of growth. For anyone with Asian land-based or omnichannel exposure, the read is that the recovery narrative has stalled and that promotional intensity, already at record levels per recent CBRE commission analysis, is doing more of the work of holding volume.",
    "expanded": "By segment, UBS said: 'Between the segments, mass daily revenue run-rate was down 10 percent to 12 percent month-on-month; while VIP volume daily run-rate was down 8 percent to 10 percent month-on-month, at VIP hold of 3.0 percent to 3.3 percent.' August GGR was just over MOP 21.89bn, down 1.2% year on year but up 8.1% sequentially, marking a third straight month of annual decline after 16 months of growth. Consensus for full-September average daily GGR of MOP 650m to MOP 670m implies 7% to 10% year-on-year growth, so the market still expects the month to finish ahead of last year despite the weak opening week. UBS also flagged softer October Golden Week indicators for the 1-7 October period: of 31 hotels tracked, five fewer are sold out year on year, and average comparable hotel prices are down 22% year on year. Hotel pricing is generally a better forward indicator of Macau visitation than booking counts, since operators discount to fill rather than leave rooms empty, and a 22% decline suggests concessionaires are already positioning for weaker demand rather than being surprised by it.",
    "source": "https://www.ggrasia.com/macau-casino-ggr-in-early-sept-tracks-seasonal-softness-ubs",
