    "meta": "iGaming Business | 8 Sep 2026",
    "summary": "iGame Media has launched OneData, an odds and sports data gateway giving sportsbooks, platforms and prediction markets access to multiple specialist providers through a single integration and one commercial access model. The launch supplier list is 10Star, Abelson Sports, ALT Sports Data, Betinvest, Huddle, Oval Insights, Sail GP, Sporting Solutions, Sporting Risk, SWA and Twenty First Group. The ecosystem spans more than 30 sports and over 1,000,000 events per year across four betting formats, fixed odds, expectancies, bet builder and live event data, delivered in under 100 milliseconds. It is underpinned by OneMap, iGame's unified ID engine mapping every provider's teams, leagues, markets and events.",
    "why": "The genuine cost in specialist data is rarely the feed licence; it is the integration and the perpetual maintenance as each provider changes its schema, plus the entity-resolution work of mapping teams, leagues and markets across sources. OneMap is the part of this worth attention, because a unified ID layer across eleven providers is the hard problem and it is what makes supplier substitution cheap rather than merely possible. If iGame's technical team absorbs feed updates 'with zero interruption and time spent by the operator', the effect is to convert a fixed engineering commitment into a variable commercial one, which changes what niche sports and emerging odds models are worth attempting. The aggregation-of-aggregators pattern is also becoming a recognisable competitive threat in sportsbook data, the same way content aggregation reshaped casino supply, and it deserves watching as a distribution model.",
    "expanded": "Customers choose which suppliers they consume inside OneData and can request additional supplier integrations, with iGame Media's technical team implementing supplier feed updates 'with zero interruption and time spent by the operator'. The company says the same approach in its live streaming platform already removes individual integrations and ongoing maintenance for 20-plus streaming suppliers, 'saving development teams hundreds of hours every single year'. The pitch targets both feed integration cost and maintenance drag, and the unlocking of niche sports, emerging odds models and products previously blocked from roadmaps. The explicit inclusion of prediction markets in the target customer list is notable, since exchange and event-contract venues need pricing and settlement data for the same underlyings as sportsbooks but have generally had to build supplier relationships from scratch. Mike Cobain, founder and CEO of iGame Media, said: 'iGame Media has spent over 10 years as the Swiss army knife of video to this industry, with 150+ direct integrations with the world's leading operators... OneData is the next organic step in that evolution. A single integration providing access to an ecosystem of laser focused odds and data providers.' More suppliers and sports are promised, with demonstrations at SBC Summit.",
