    "section": "Product",
    "title": "BETBY launches SlotBets, converting live basketball events into 15-second three-reel rounds it brands a new slotbetting category",
    "meta": "SBC News | 8 Sep 2026",
    "summary": "B2B sportsbook supplier BETBY has launched SlotBets, which converts sports betting into slot-style gameplay and integrates sportsbook and casino into one experience, a category BETBY labels slotbetting. The format is built around 15-second betting rounds tied directly to a live sporting event. Each round is divided into three five-second windows representing three reels; each reel highlights the highest-value event occurring within its window, a three-pointer, two-pointer, missed shot, foul, or a period of no action. After 15 seconds, matching outcome combinations across the three reels produce payouts per the paytable, substituting RNG mechanics entirely for real-world events.",
    "why": "The design question this answers is the one every sportsbook-casino crossover has struggled with, which is how to give a casino player sports exposure without requiring sports knowledge. Kirill Nekrasov's framing is unusually clear about that: 'why should a casino player need to become a sportsbook expert before they can enjoy betting on sport?' The engineering implications are real, though. Replacing RNG with live event outcomes means the paytable's return to player is a function of in-play event frequency distributions, which vary by league, by game state and by officiating, so RTP verification and certification become statistical modelling exercises rather than fixed calculations. Latency and settlement integrity on five-second windows also demand event feeds and dispute handling well beyond normal in-play tolerances. Whether regulators will treat this as a casino game or a sports bet is an open and consequential question.",
    "expanded": "Basketball was chosen as the first sport for its fast-paced dynamic, with eligible stoppages contributing via a Pause Bonus that adds towards payout multipliers. Kirill Nekrasov, Head of Innovation and R&D at BETBY, said: 'SlotBets started with a very simple question: why should a casino player need to become a sportsbook expert before they can enjoy betting on sport? We wanted to create something immediately understandable, but still genuinely powered by the live event. That is why the sport cannot simply be decoration around a casino mechanic. Every basket, miss, foul, stoppage or quiet interval can influence the game, so the match is continuously building the SlotBet in real time.' He added: 'We believe SlotBets Games can develop its own recognisable mechanics, terminology and player expectations, in the same way that categories such as Crash Games did before.' The Crash comparison is apt and instructive, since Crash established that a genuinely new mechanic can create its own category and its own player expectations within a few years, but it also arrived with significant regulatory ambiguity about classification. SlotBets will be showcased at BETBY's stand at SBC Summit Lisbon, and follows the company's integrated video-betting launch on 20 August 2026.",
