    "summary": "Continent 8 Technologies has extended its partnership with Nutanix and been selected as an early access partner to help shape Nutanix Service Provider Central, a new multitenant cloud platform first announced in April 2026. Continent 8 will be among the first service providers worldwide to deploy a service leveraging SP Central commercially, combining Nutanix's multitenant capabilities with Continent 8's operational governance model to maintain control and oversight across individual customer environments. The named customer proof point is Sportingtech, where Continent 8 led a VMware-to-Nutanix migration that avoided a significant projected rise in virtualisation costs while preserving security, performance and compliance posture.",
    "why": "The Sportingtech migration is the detail with immediate relevance, because Broadcom's VMware licensing changes have raised virtualisation costs across the industry and iGaming platforms are unusually exposed given their regulated-market requirement to run isolated, certified environments per jurisdiction. Multiplying licence cost by jurisdiction count is how a licensing change becomes a material P&L item. A documented migration path that preserves compliance posture while avoiding that increase is therefore worth understanding in detail rather than dismissing as vendor content, particularly the question of how certification and regulator-approved environment isolation were maintained through the hypervisor change. Note this piece is carried as an advertising feature, so the cost-avoidance claim is unquantified and comes from the supplier. Still, the underlying pressure is real and the multitenancy angle speaks directly to how per-jurisdiction environments are provisioned and governed.",
    "expanded": "The announcement cites Continent 8's certified cloud specialists and AI-enabled Global Capability Centres in India, the Philippines and Bulgaria supporting large-scale cloud migrations and infrastructure modernisation. Mike Small, CEO at Continent 8 Technologies, said extending the partnership 'reinforces our commitment to helping iGaming customers modernise with confidence, simplify operations, optimise costs and prepare for the next generation of digital services, cloud-native applications and AI-driven innovation'. Edward O'Connor, CTO at Continent 8, said the relationship 'is much deeper than a traditional vendor relationship' with engineering and product teams working 'side-by-side' for several years. Sachin Chheda, VP of business development and strategic partnerships at Nutanix, said: 'By leveraging the Nutanix Cloud Platform and SP Central and their multitenant capabilities, Continent 8 is equipped to deliver the operational simplicity, security, and performance that their customers demand and need.' Early access partner status means Continent 8 will influence the product's roadmap before general availability, which matters for iGaming-specific requirements around tenant isolation, audit logging and jurisdictional data residency that general-purpose cloud platforms rarely address natively.",
